# sys-dig: Dig from the party menu (decomp field_move_tasks.c FieldMoves_CheckDig and FieldMoves_DigTask,
# overlay006/field_warp.c sDigTeleportStates). With a Diglett knowing Dig: refused on Route 203 (not a cave:
# PartyMenu_Text_CantUseThatHere). In Oreburgh Gate, a cave whose header allows an Escape Rope, after a save round
# trip: Teleport's cut-in, spin and fade, then the exit recorded when the player walked in (as an Escape Rope), on foot.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_DIGLETT 20 platinum:MOVE_DIG
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_203 246 749 right
+0 wild flee
until idle
+1 press x
+1 release x
until app start-menu
+1 tap entry:0
+1 tap slot:0
+1 tap menu:1
+1 assert app party
+0 assert text platinum:PartyMenu_Text_CantUseThatHere 0
+1 press a
+1 release a
+1 press b
+1 release b
+1 press b
+1 release b
until app none
until idle
+0 press right
+1 release right
until state player.zone "platinum:MAP_HEADER_OREBURGH_GATE_1F"
advance text
until idle
+0 reload
until idle
+1 press x
+1 release x
until app start-menu
+1 tap entry:0
+1 tap slot:0
+1 tap menu:1
until app none
until idle 600
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_203 246 749
+0 assert state playerState "walk"
